---
import MainLayout from "../layouts/MainLayout.astro";

const pageTitle = "The Loop — References & Further Reading";
const description =
  "Academic sources, research papers, and further reading that informed the content of The Loop.";
---

<MainLayout title={pageTitle} description={description}>
  <section class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-4xl flex-col gap-10 px-4 py-12">

    <!-- Intro -->
    <article class="relative overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-slate-700/80 bg-slate-900/70 px-6 py-8 shadow-lg">
      <div class="mb-4 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-sky-300">
        <span class="h-px w-6 bg-sky-400/70"></span>
        References
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-100 md:text-xl">
        <p>
          The content of <strong>The Loop</strong> is grounded in paper research.
        </p>

        <p>
          The sources below informed the explanations, examples, and ethical discussions
          throughout the website.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>

    <!-- References list -->
    <article class="max-w-prose space-y-6 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-200 md:text-lg">

      <ul class="space-y-4">

        <li>
          <a href="https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/american-journal-of-law-and-medicine/article/algorithms-addiction-and-adolescent-mental-health-an-interdisciplinary-study-to-inform-statelevel-policy-action-to-protect-youth-from-the-dangers-of-social-media/EC9754B533553BDD56827CD9E34DFC25">
            Costello, C., et al. (2023) <em>Algorithms, Addiction, and Adolescent Mental Health:
            An Interdisciplinary Study to Inform State-Level Policy Action</em>.
            <span class="italic">American Journal of Law & Medicine</span>.
          </a>
        </li>

        <li>
          <a href="https://assets.cureus.com/uploads/review_article/pdf/109723/20240724-319105-cem048.pdf">
            Gupta, R. (2021) <em>The Impact of Social Media on Mental Health</em>.
          </a>
        </li>

        <li>
            <a href="https://assets.cureus.com/uploads/review_article/pdf/176889/20230904-18910-555yiy.pdf">
                Khalaf, O. (2023) <em>The Impact of Social Media on Mental Health: A Systematic Review</em>.
            </a>
        </li>

        <li>
            <a href="https://academiccommons.columbia.edu/doi/10.7916/khdk-m460">
                Narayanan, A. (2023) <em>Understanding Social Media Recommendation Algorithms</em>.
            </a>
        </li>

        <li>
            <a href="https://soc.gpmsh.ac.ir/article_212042.html">
                Nosraty, S. (2021) <em>The Impact of Social Media on Mental Health: A Critical Examination</em>.
            </a>
        </li>

        <li>
          <a href="https://www.shs-conferences.org/articles/shsconf/pdf/2024/05/shsconf_iclcc2024_03008.pdf">
            Qiu, L. (2024) <em>Social Comparison on Social Media Platforms: A Media and Communication
           Perspective</em>.
          </a>
        </li>

        <li>
          <a href="https://www.mdpi.com/2075-4698/15/11/301">
            Ahmmad, M., et al. (2025) <em>Trap of Social Media Algorithms: A Systematic Review of
            Research on Filter Bubbles, Echo Chambers, and Their Impact on Youth</em>.
          </a>
        </li>

        <li>
          <a href="https://stars.library.ucf.edu/honorstheses1990-2015/1684/">
            Strickland, R. (2022) <em>Exploring the Effects of Social Media Use on the Mental Health
            of Young Adults</em>.
          </a>
        </li>

      </ul>

    </article>

    <article class="relative overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-slate-700/80 bg-slate-900/70 px-6 py-8 shadow-lg">
      <div class="mb-4 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-sky-300">
        <span class="h-px w-6 bg-sky-400/70"></span>
        Disclaimer
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-200 md:text-lg">
        <p>
          If for any reason the papers refered to in this work aren't available online or the links do not work, they can be provided upon requested as I do have them all saved locally.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>

    <!-- Closing -->
    <article class="max-w-prose space-y-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-200 md:text-lg">
      <p>
        Social media platforms are complex systems shaped by technical design, economic
        incentives, and human behaviour.
      </p>

      <p>
        Understanding these systems does not require rejecting technology altogether —
        it requires awareness, critical thinking, and informed discussion.
      </p>

      <p>
        <strong>The Loop</strong> aims to contribute to that conversation.
      </p>
    </article>

  </section>
</MainLayout>
